### Rationale
E3 is refuted. At every L size the 128-bit parent was the fastest variant, so I'm returning the parent kernel with its code unchanged.

I timed all six variants on the rented B200 with `harness_time` (7 interleaved reps, medians). The 256-bit loads and stores came out 1–3% slower than the parent, as did the two-stream ordering.

